From b5129c205af06471fad41e28571a94d9dae2f8be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 05:00:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] stage-1.1-cors-and-cache: strip wildcard CORS from HTML,
 ISR on static hubs

Production was measured serving headers that exist in no file here:

  $ curl -sI https://greenhardwood.ca/
  access-control-allow-origin: *
  cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

The wildcard comes from the Vercel project's dashboard header config, so
it is outside version control and outside review. A wildcard ACAO on a
marketing page lets any origin read the rendered document cross-origin
and is a standing finding on every security scan run against the domain.

middleware.ts now deletes it from every response except the deliberate
agent surfaces (/api/*, /card.vcf, /.well-known/*, llms.txt, llms-full.txt,
ai.txt, feed.xml), which keep it. isCorsPublicPath() is pinned by tests so
nobody can quietly add a page to that list.

ISR revalidate=3600 on /, /stairs, /services, /areas, /about, /faq and
/portfolio so the edge serves s-maxage + stale-while-revalidate rather
than must-revalidate.

Removing the header from the Vercel dashboard is tracked as an off-site
blocker; the code no longer depends on someone remembering to.

