From aa71cbfba6bf2811aeaccfaeb0a14565b2f90b60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 05:00:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] stage-2-measurement: GTM, GA4-via-GTM, Vercel vitals,
 typed event taxonomy
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You cannot dominate what you cannot see. The site had no analytics of
any kind: no GTM, no GA4, no pixels, no RUM.

- lib/analytics.ts: the whole event taxonomy as one typed union. A call
  site cannot invent an event name no GTM trigger listens for.
  CONVERSION_EVENTS is exactly tel_click, sms_click, estimate_submit.
- components/analytics/gtm.tsx: GTM only, gated on NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID,
  afterInteractive. No second gtag.js anywhere — a test enforces that,
  because two tags on one page double every conversion count.
- components/analytics/click-tracker.tsx: ONE delegated capture-phase
  listener covers every tel:, sms:, outbound, portfolio and download
  link on all 371 pages, including links not written yet. The
  alternative was ~500 onClick edits and a client boundary pushed into
  server-rendered chrome that currently ships no JS.
- @vercel/analytics + @vercel/speed-insights: real pageviews and field
  Core Web Vitals from day one, before any GTM container exists. Field
  vitals are the only honest check on the Stage 1 LCP work.
- estimate_start on first control touch; estimate_band_shown debounced
  700ms so one slider drag is one event, not a hundred.
- estimate_submit fires from the SERVER action's success verdict via a
  new LeadAnalytics type, not from onSubmit. Validation bounces and
  honeypot catches therefore cannot inflate the lead count.

Privacy is a type, not a convention: LeadAnalytics carries city slug,
service kind and source only. A test fails the build if a parameter
named name/email/phone/address/message ever appears in the taxonomy.

docs/analytics.md ships the full GTM container recipe, the content-group
lookup table, and a verification walk whose key step is confirming an
INVALID submit fires no conversion.

